    {
      "slug": "portinari-altarpiece",
      "title": "Portinari Altarpiece",
      "year": 1475,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Hugo_van_der_Goes_-_Portinari_Triptych_%28c._1477%29.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 3928,
      "imageHeight": 1630,
      "story": "The Portinari Altarpiece or Portinari Triptych is an oil-on-wood triptych painting by the Flemish painter Hugo van der Goes, commissioned by Tommaso Portinari, representing the Adoration of the Shepherds. It measures 253 x 304 cm, and is now in the Galleria degli Uffizi in Florence, Italy.",
      "facts": [
        "The work was commissioned for the church inside of one of the largest hospitals in Florence, hospital of Santa Maria Nuova by the Italian banker Tommaso Portinari, a descendant of the hospital's founder.",
        "Hugo van der Goes's Altarpiece is considered to have some of the most complicated and hidden symbolism in any Nativity scene from the fifteenth century."
      ],
